<text x="170.0" y="88" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#8b949e" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="400" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:2.10s">FORMULA</text>
<text x="306" y="88" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#3fb950" text-anchor="end" font-weight="600" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:2.45s">Σₖ A[i,k]·B[k,j]</text>
<line x1="32" y1="96" x2="308" y2="96" stroke="#30363d" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="38" y="114" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="12" fill="#f0f6fc" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:2.80s">cost</text>
<text x="170.0" y="114" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#8b949e" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="400" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:3.15s">BIG-O</text>
<text x="306" y="114" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#3fb950" text-anchor="end" font-weight="600" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:3.50s">O(m·n·p)</text>
<line x1="32" y1="122" x2="308" y2="122" stroke="#30363d" stroke-width="1"/>
<text x="38" y="140" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="12" fill="#f0f6fc" text-anchor="start" font-weight="400" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:3.85s">AB vs BA</text>
<text x="170.0" y="140" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#8b949e" text-anchor="middle" font-weight="400" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:4.20s">FACT</text>
<text x="306" y="140" font-family="ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,SF Mono,Menlo,Consolas,monospace" font-size="11" fill="#3fb950" text-anchor="end" font-weight="600" opacity="1.0" class="a-node" style="animation-delay:4.55s">not equal, usually</text></svg><figcaption style="margin-top:.6em;color:#8b949e;font-size:.85em;text-align:center"><strong>Fig. il12-math-linalg-D2 — </strong>Matrix multiplication composes linear maps: each entry of C is a dot product of a row of A with a column of B. Order matters — AB ≠ BA in general — because applying rotation then scaling differs from scaling then rotation.</figcaption></figure>

Eigenvalues solve det(A − λI) = 0. For A=[[1, 2], [3, 4]]: (1−λ)(4−λ) − 6 = λ² − 5λ + (-2) ... precisely λ² − (trace)λ + det = 0, i.e. λ² − 5λ + -2 = 0. Discriminant 5² − 4×-2 = **33**. λ = (5 ± √33)/2 = **5.3723**, **-0.3723**. Check: λ₁+λ₂ = 5.0000 = trace ✓; λ₁×λ₂ = -2.0000 = det ✓. Eigenvalues are the scaling factors along the matrix's natural axes — the basis of PCA and stability analysis.

<figure class="il-diagram" style="margin:1.2em 0"><svg viewBox="0 0 720 184" width="100%" role="img" aria-label="Concept box: eigenvalues via trace and determinant" class="il-anim" style="display:block;max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;background:#0d1117;border-radius:10px"><rect width="720" height="184" fill="#0d1117" rx="10"/>
<style>
