Write a statistical audit of a published-style claim I provide (a model 'beats baseline by 2%' on a small test set, with no intervals or significance reported). Deliverable: a short report that (1) recomputes the comparison with confidence intervals, (2) states whether the difference is statistically distinguishable from noise, (3) checks the sample for plausible bias sources, and (4) gives a verdict: real improvement, inconclusive, or misleading — with the math shown. Grading bar: a verdict of 'real improvement' without intervals fails; the whole point is that the original claim is unevaluated.

