Build a SQL validation-and-feature pack for a dataset I provide (events + users tables with planted defects: duplicate keys, null foreign keys, future timestamps, a broken session boundary). Deliverable: a single .sql file with (1) a validation section that catches every planted defect with a labeled query, (2) a feature section producing a model-ready per-user table via CTEs and window functions, and (3) a README stating the grain of each output and the row-count audit. Grading bar: miss a planted defect and it fails — and any query whose grain you can't state in one sentence gets rewritten.

