Tuning report on a dataset I provide: define a search space with justification, run randomized search inside leak-proof pipelines with stratified CV, compare against a grid baseline on equal budget, and report the winner with a nested-CV unbiased estimate. Include the deliberate-leakage experiment (preprocessing outside the fold) with measured inflation. Grading bar: the final reported number must come from data untouched by tuning — a 'best validation score' presented as the result fails.

