Engineer context on a long-horizon task. Measure tokens and success together — that's the discipline.
1. **Rot it.** Run an agent task with ever-growing context (no management); plot success vs context length. Watch the rot — the empirical motive for everything after.
2. **Compact it.** Implement transcript summarization at intervals; compare task success vs the unmanaged run and vs full history. The degradation (or lack of it), measured.
3. **Clear the tools.** Drop bulky tool payloads post-use, keeping call records; measure token savings and success delta. Re-fetchable beats retained — verify.
4. **Structure memory.** Move durable facts to an external note store with just-in-time retrieval; compare against stuffing everything in context. The window holds the now.
5. **Set the altitude.** Audit a system prompt: move task-state down to working context, keep durable rules up. Measure the token and focus effects of correct altitude.
6. **A/B the strategies.** Two context designs head-to-head on the same long task: tokens used, success rate, cost. Context design is empirical — run the experiment.

