Instrument a real LLM system and debug it from traces. The trace is the debugger.
1. **Trace the system.** Instrument an LLM app (agent or RAG) with span tracing; run ten queries and read every trace. The execution, made visible — feel the difference from metrics.
2. **Find the expensive span.** Break down cost and latency per span type; identify the dominant cost (usually one model call or retrieval pattern). The attribution that drives optimization.
3. **Debug from a trace.** Take a failing run; diagnose from the trace alone (wrong tool args? bad retrieval? loop?). The trace-as-debugger skill, practiced.
4. **Build the dashboard.** Cost, latency, quality across runs: the three panels with per-span drill-down. The operational view, built.
5. **Trace-to-dataset.** Export failing traces into an eval set with labels; re-run after a fix and show the delta. Production failures becoming regression tests.
6. **Detect automatically.** Implement one automated detector (loop detection, cost spike, error cascade) over the trace stream; tune it on historical traces. Alerting on behavior.

