Pipelines automate both good and bad practice — gates, validation, and rollback are what make automation safe, and they're the parts teams skip. Complexity has a cost: pipeline infrastructure is worth it when retraining is frequent, overkill for one-off models. No certificate is conferred; the durable principle is gates that block.

