Frame three candidate capstones; commit to one. The framing document is the deliverable.
1. **Generate candidates.** Five capstone ideas; run each through the three filters (scoped, substantial, demonstrable). Kill two in writing — the kill reasoning is the skill.
2. **Metric first.** For the survivors, define success metrics before any data exploration. Get the metric agreed (with yourself, on paper) — no moving goalposts later.
3. **Audit the data.** Full inventory for the top candidate: sources, access, quality sample, licensing, gaps and their cost. The audit decides feasibility — read it honestly.
4. **Baseline the feasibility.** The simplest end-to-end run proving solvability. If the baseline can't beat trivial, the project needs re-scoping — decide now, cheaply.
5. **Scope to finish.** Milestones, dates, cut lines, minimum viable demo. Then cut 30% — the re-scope that saves capstones.
6. **Pre-check ethics.** Harms, bias, misuse: the responsible-AI review of your own idea before week two. Document the mitigations in the framing doc.

