Self-review is the hardest review — the temptation to grade your own work generously is the bias to watch. Documented limits build trust; hidden ones destroy it when found. Responsibility doesn't end at ship; monitoring for harm is ongoing. No certificate is conferred; the product is the habit distinguishing engineers from demo artists.

