- **Time horizon (P50/P80)** — The human-expert task length at which an agent has a 50% (or 80%) chance of success, read off a logistic curve fitted to model success vs. human task length (METR).
- **Logistic fit** — Plot success probability against human task length, fit the curve, read the 50% crossing. That crossing is your ceiling.
- **Doubling: 195.8 days** — The 50%-reliability horizon doubled roughly every 7 months from 2019–2025 (95% CI [162, 223] days).
- **TH1.1 post-2023: 130.8 days** — METR's January 2026 refresh finds the recent doubling 20% faster (95% CI [107, 161]) — ceilings move in months, not years.
- **Suite sensitivity** — Horizons are fitted, suite-specific estimates. Change the task mix and the number moves.
- **Reliability ceiling** — An engineering boundary: no unsupervised subtask longer than the measured P50 without decomposition or human checkpoints.
- **Autonomy ceiling** — The design rule this module teaches: the ceiling is a boundary, not a target.

